From: MATYJAGUZ075 <matyjaguz075@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gd/hci: no abortar con COMMAND_COMPLETE sin comando en espera

El bluetooth se desconectaba solo mientras se usaba. Causa medida en el
telefono (tombstone_00, 2026-11-13 10:22:52):

  Cmdline: com.android.bluetooth
  pid: 3243, tid: 3411, name: bt_stack_manage
  signal 6 (SIGABRT)
  Abort message: 'assertion 'op_code == OpCode::NONE' failed - Received
  COMMAND_COMPLETE event with OpCode 0xd425 (Unknown OpCode: 54309) without
  a waiting command(is the HAL sending commands, but not handling the events?)'
      #04 libbluetooth_jni.so (bluetooth::hci::HciLayer::impl::on_hci_event)

El stack GD de A13 exige que, cuando no hay comando en espera, el
COMMAND_COMPLETE/STATUS traiga el opcode 0 (NONE, control de flujo). El HAL
legacy de este dispositivo (BCM43438 con el HAL de Samsung) responde con su
propio opcode (0xd425) a comandos que el stack no ha enviado, y el
ASSERT_LOG() (LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL) mataba el proceso com.android.bluetooth.

El parche 003 ya toleraba los asserts de handle_command_response; este cubre
el camino de on_hci_event, que es por donde llega el evento en este caso.
Los dos ASSERT_LOG pasan a LOG_WARN y los ASSERT(view.IsValid()) a un
warning con descarte del evento: el stack sigue vivo y el bluetooth deja de
caerse.

Nota: no es un problema de memoria. En el mismo arranque no hay ningun OOM
ni lowmemorykiller en /proc/last_kmsg, y el abort es un SIGABRT del propio
stack de bluetooth.

---
diff --git a/system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc b/system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc
index 4e341ba..dae752a 100644
--- a/system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc
+++ b/system/gd/hci/hci_layer.cc
@@ -357,21 +357,39 @@ struct HciLayer::impl {
       // COMMAND_COMPLETE and COMMAND_STATUS with opcode 0x0 for flow control
       if (event_code == EventCode::COMMAND_COMPLETE) {
           auto view = CommandCompleteView::Create(event);
-          ASSERT(view.IsValid());
+          if (!view.IsValid()) {
+            // Evento malformado: ASSERT() abortaba el proceso.
+            LOG_WARN("Invalid COMMAND_COMPLETE event without a waiting command, discarding");
+            return;
+          }
           auto op_code = view.GetCommandOpCode();
-          ASSERT_LOG(op_code == OpCode::NONE,
-            "Received %s event with OpCode 0x%02hx (%s) without a waiting command"
-            "(is the HAL sending commands, but not handling the events?)",
-            EventCodeText(event_code).c_str(), op_code, OpCodeText(op_code).c_str());
+          if (op_code != OpCode::NONE) {
+            // El HAL legacy de este dispositivo (BCM43438 via el HAL de
+            // Samsung) responde con su propio opcode a comandos que el stack
+            // de A13 no ha enviado. Medido en el telefono:
+            //   Abort message: 'assertion 'op_code == OpCode::NONE' failed -
+            //   Received COMMAND_COMPLETE event with OpCode 0xd425
+            //   (Unknown OpCode: 54309) without a waiting command
+            //   (is the HAL sending commands, but not handling the events?)'
+            // ASSERT_LOG() usa LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL: abortaba el proceso
+            // com.android.bluetooth y el bluetooth se caia (se desconectaba
+            // solo mientras se usaba). Se degrada a warning: el evento se
+            // registra y se ignora, el stack sigue vivo.
+            LOG_WARN("Received %s event with OpCode 0x%04hx (%s) without a waiting command",
+                     EventCodeText(event_code).c_str(), op_code, OpCodeText(op_code).c_str());
+          }
       }
       if (event_code == EventCode::COMMAND_STATUS) {
           auto view = CommandStatusView::Create(event);
-          ASSERT(view.IsValid());
+          if (!view.IsValid()) {
+            LOG_WARN("Invalid COMMAND_STATUS event without a waiting command, discarding");
+            return;
+          }
           auto op_code = view.GetCommandOpCode();
-          ASSERT_LOG(op_code == OpCode::NONE,
-            "Received %s event with OpCode 0x%02hx (%s) without a waiting command"
-            "(is the HAL sending commands, but not handling the events?)",
-            EventCodeText(event_code).c_str(), op_code, OpCodeText(op_code).c_str());
+          if (op_code != OpCode::NONE) {
+            LOG_WARN("Received %s event with OpCode 0x%04hx (%s) without a waiting command",
+                     EventCodeText(event_code).c_str(), op_code, OpCodeText(op_code).c_str());
+          }
       }
       std::unique_ptr<CommandView> no_waiting_command{nullptr};
       log_hci_event(no_waiting_command, event, module_.GetDependency<storage::StorageModule>());
